{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000, acc≈0.485), the dominant uncertainty is whether adding image information provides meaningful gain over RNA alone — the central question in a multimodal cellular profiling study. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) keeps the RNA side identical to config_001 and introduces the simplest image encoder (ResNet-50) with the simplest fusion (concat), making it a clean, minimal-contrast test of 'does image information complement RNA features?' If accuracy improves substantially, it validates the multimodal direction and justifies investing subsequent experiments in richer encoders/fusion. If it does not improve, it signals that the modalities are redundant or poorly aligned under this setup, redirecting effort toward better RNA encoders or profile strategies. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the highest-leverage design axis (modality combination) before committing budget to finer-grained choices like encoder type, aggregation, or fusion strategy."
}

